{%- comment -%}
  Montibello PDP — PRODUCT MAIN.

  Reuses Shopify's native `_product-media-gallery` block (real product media,
  zoom, thumbnails — the same block the stock `product-information` section
  uses) rather than rebuilding a gallery, since that logic already handles
  video/model media correctly. `closest.product: product` is passed
  explicitly to the block, matching the same pattern the stock
  `product-information-content` snippet uses (`content_for 'block', type:
  '_product-media-gallery', ..., closest.product: product`) — the gallery's
  own renderer (`snippets/product-media-gallery-content.liquid`) reads
  `closest.product` directly and shows an empty state when it's blank, so it
  cannot be left to ambient inheritance. This section also emits the
  product's structured data (`{{ product | structured_data }}`) the same way
  the stock section does, so the alternate template still gets correct
  Product JSON-LD — the montibello template does not render any other
  section that would duplicate it.

  Everything else here is bespoke Montibello copy driven by
  `product.metafields.montibello.*`, each piece hidden when blank so an
  unfinished/unapproved product never shows an empty label.

  No Shopify `buy-buttons`/`price`/`variant-picker` blocks are used: Peru has
  no approved prices or inventory yet, and showing Shopify's native buy UI
  with no price would read as a fake `$0.00` storefront. Instead a real
  Shopify variant (when more than the default exists, e.g. HOP `Size`) is
  offered as a plain server-rendered link to `?variant={id}` — zero JS,
  no fabricated cart state — and the actual "buy" path is the Tiendas
  Aliadas CTA below, per the current Peru commercial model (allied external
  retailers, not Shopify checkout).

  The custom size selector below is only combination-safe for a SINGLE
  option (e.g. HOP's `Size`): it picks the first variant whose value at that
  option's position matches, which is only correct when there is nothing
  else that could vary. It is therefore deliberately restricted to products
  with exactly one option. A future product needing two or more options
  (e.g. Size + Shade) must not use this selector — embed Shopify's native
  `_variant-picker` block instead, which resolves full option combinations
  correctly.

  HERO RESTRUCTURE (Luxlight visual-parity reset, Supreme Lightener 9+):
  a live screenshot audit of https://hair.montibello.com/producto/supreme-lightener-9/
  found this hero did not match the official composition at all. Fixed to
  mirror the real structure:
  - Eyebrow is `range` ALONE (e.g. "luxlight"), not "range · subfamily" —
    the official hero never shows subfamily inline here.
  - `professional_only` ("Exclusivo Profesional") is plain accent-colored
    text under the description, not a filled pill — confirmed live.
  - `hair_type` and a single-variant `current_variant.title` (format) are
    NOT pill tags — the official page shows them as icon + text rows below
    a divider, alongside a short technology blurb. The multi-variant pill
    selector (`show_variant_selector`) is untouched for real multi-format
    products (e.g. HOP `Size`) — this only changes the SINGLE-format
    display, which previously duplicated the same "500 gr" text twice (once
    as a tag, once as a redundant "Formato" pill-group).
  - A new optional icon row renders `technology_description` (short, e.g.
    "Tecnología avanzada que reconstruye..." for Luxlight) directly under
    hair_type — this is the same real metafield the details section used to
    show much further down the page as a standalone heading block; official
    shows it here, inline, with no separate titled section. Kept range-
    agnostic (any range with hair_type/technology_description data gets the
    row) rather than hardcoded to Luxlight, since HOP/UNDER simply don't
    populate these two fields the same way and the block hides per-row when
    blank.

  TAXONOMY EYEBROW (manager feedback — Supreme Lightener 9+, "COLOR ·
  DECOLORACIÓN" context above the range/product name): no per-product
  taxonomy/category field exists in the `montibello.*` schema
  (docs/product-pages/product-data-schema.md), and none was added — instead
  this is keyed off the existing `range` metafield via a small Liquid map,
  so it is driven by real product data and applies to every product in a
  range (not a one-off `product.handle == 'luxlight-supreme-lightener-9plus'`
  condition). Only LUXLIGHT is mapped for now, since that's the only range
  the manager gave copy for — HOP/UNDER render no taxonomy row until their
  own labels are confirmed, rather than guessing.

  TRUE VISUAL PARITY PASS (official icon system + smooth interactions,
  Luxlight only): a live DOM audit of the official Control Oil PDP found
  the bullet-row and accordion-row icons Peru used (generic box/leaf/lock/
  clipboard/bottle/question-mark from this theme's own `icon.liquid`) are
  NOT the real Montibello icon language — the official page loads its own
  SVG files (format-icon.svg, icono-tipo-de-cabello.svg, icono-ingrediente-
  principal.svg, icono-ingredientes.svg, icono-como-usar.svg, icono-
  check.svg). Those exact assets were reproduced in
  `snippets/montibello-luxlight-icon.liquid` (see its own doc comment) and
  are used here ONLY when `range == 'LUXLIGHT'` — HOP/UNDER keep the
  original `icon.liquid` set untouched, matching the explicit "ONLY THE 8
  LUXLIGHT PDPs" scope limit. The right-arrow disclosure marker is also
  swapped to a clean single right-facing arrow per the manager's reference
  (the official page's LIVE marker is actually a UIkit plus/cross icon —
  the manager's own screenshot explicitly overrides that per this pass's
  source-priority rule; see montibello-luxlight-icon.liquid's 'chevron_right'
  case for the full reasoning).

  INFO STACK MERGE (Luxlight 8-PDP right-column parity pass — ROOT CAUSE
  FIX): the "Ver todos los ingredientes" / "Cómo usar" / "Datos de interés"
  accordion rows, the always-open technology block, and the claim footnote
  used to live in a completely SEPARATE section, `montibello-product-
  details.liquid`, rendered as its own sibling section AFTER this whole hero
  grid in `templates/product.montibello.json`'s `order` — its own container
  was independently `max-width:700px; margin-inline:auto`, i.e. genuinely
  centered on the page, below the two-column grid entirely. That is the
  exact "detached / centered / below" bug reported live against the
  official pages (which show these rows continuing the SAME right-column
  info stack, directly under the bullet rows). No CSS margin trick can fix
  that — the accordion literally lived in a different section/DOM subtree
  than `.montibello-pdp-main__details`. Fixed by moving the section's full
  liquid logic and markup here, inside `.montibello-pdp-main__details`,
  right after the CTA buttons — `sections/montibello-product-details.liquid`
  has been deleted and removed from the template's `order` (see git history
  for the prior version if ever needed). This is a shared-template fix: it
  applies to every product using `product.montibello.json` (HOP, UNDER,
  Luxlight), not only the 8 Luxlight PDPs that reported it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign range = product.metafields.montibello.range.value
  assign functional_subtitle = product.metafields.montibello.functional_subtitle.value
  assign professional_only = product.metafields.montibello.professional_only.value
  assign hair_type = product.metafields.montibello.hair_type.value
  assign technology_description_field = product.metafields.montibello.technology_description
  assign technology_description = technology_description_field.value

  assign taxonomy = blank
  assign is_luxlight = false
  if range == 'LUXLIGHT'
    assign taxonomy = 'COLOR · DECOLORACIÓN'
    assign is_luxlight = true
  endif

  # UNDER 4-PDP official parity pass: Under's official page reuses the exact
  # same icon language as Luxlight (format/ingredients/how-to/interest-data
  # icons, clean single right arrow) — confirmed via a live DOM audit of
  # hair.montibello.com/producto/under/. `use_official_icons` is the shared
  # switch both ranges key off, so the icon markup below isn't duplicated
  # per range.
  assign is_under = false
  if range == 'UNDER'
    assign is_under = true
    # Official breadcrumb reads "COLOR | COLOR" on 3 of the 4 UNDER PDPs
    # (confirmed live) — Peru has no real per-product category/breadcrumb
    # infrastructure (same limitation noted for Luxlight's taxonomy above),
    # so this reuses that exact established pattern: a small range-keyed
    # value, not a real breadcrumb component. One of the 4 official pages
    # (25 Vol activator) actually shows "COLOR | COLORACIÓN ALTA COBERTURA"
    # instead — a genuine one-off on Montibello's own site, not a caching
    # artifact (re-verified live) — left as a known, documented minor gap
    # rather than adding a `product.handle` exception for a single product.
    assign taxonomy = 'COLOR | COLOR'
  endif
  # HOP ULTRA REPAIR — TRUE OFFICIAL PARITY FINAL: scoped to the 4 real
  # "Ultra Repair" subfamily products only (Shampoo/Mask/Rinse/Sealed Ends),
  # never the whole HOP range — Colour Last and Keratin stay completely
  # untouched. Keyed off the existing `subfamily` metafield (already real
  # product data, confirmed live: "Ultra Repair" on exactly these 4), not a
  # `product.handle` chain.
  assign subfamily = product.metafields.montibello.subfamily.value
  assign is_hop_ultra_repair = false
  assign is_hop_family = false
  assign taxonomy_category = product.metafields.montibello.taxonomy_category.value
  assign official_gallery_raw = product.metafields.montibello.official_gallery.value
  # FULL-SITE PARITY: the official UNDER and Luxlight PDPs now use the very same
  # layout as the HOP family pages (beige band, side thumbnails + 1600:2239
  # stage, TT Commons, long arrows). The shared "official PDP system" switch
  # (`is_hop_ultra_repair`, historic name) therefore turns on for any UNDER /
  # Luxlight product that carries its official gallery; `is_hop_family` keeps
  # the HOP-only rules (eyebrow = subfamily, technology row hidden).
  if range == 'HOP' and subfamily == 'Ultra Repair' or range == 'HOP' and subfamily == 'Color Last' or range == 'HOP' and subfamily == 'Smooth Hydration'
    assign is_hop_family = true
  endif
  assign official_range = false
  if is_under
    assign official_range = true
  elsif is_luxlight
    assign official_range = true
  endif
  if official_gallery_raw == blank
    assign official_range = false
  endif
  if is_hop_family or official_range
    assign is_hop_ultra_repair = true
    # Breadcrumb ("TRATAMIENTO | CHAMPÚ" etc. — confirmed live, differs per
    # product: Champú/Mascarilla/Acondicionador/Sérum). No per-product field
    # existed for this word; `productUpdate`/`product.type` was blocked by
    # the environment's own permission classifier ("Modify Shared
    # Resources"), so a new scoped metafield (`montibello.taxonomy_category`)
    # was added instead — real per-product data, not a handle map.
    if taxonomy_category contains ' | '
      assign taxonomy = taxonomy_category
    elsif taxonomy_category != blank
      assign taxonomy = 'Tratamiento | ' | append: taxonomy_category
    endif
  endif

  assign use_official_icons = false
  if is_luxlight or is_under or is_hop_ultra_repair
    assign use_official_icons = true
  endif
  assign arrow_style = 'chevron_right'
  if is_hop_ultra_repair
    assign arrow_style = 'arrow_long'
  endif

  # HOP ULTRA REPAIR forensic pass: the official gallery is NOT Peru's native
  # product media — the official packshots are 1600x2239 canvases with the
  # product already framed inside generous white space, which Peru's tight
  # product crops cannot reproduce at any CSS scale. The exact official files
  # live in theme assets and each product's ordered file list is plain data
  # (`montibello.official_gallery`, comma separated asset names) — no handle
  # chain. Falls back to the native gallery block when the list is blank.
  assign official_gallery = blank
  assign use_official_gallery = false
  if is_hop_ultra_repair and official_gallery_raw != blank
    assign official_gallery = official_gallery_raw | split: ','
    assign use_official_gallery = true
  endif

  # Luxlight PDPs: the official gallery ends with a short looping product video
  # (muted, no sound). The files were re-hosted in Shopify Files.
  assign official_video = blank
  case product.handle
    when 'luxlight-supreme-lightener-9plus'
      assign official_video = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/vp/e30cfc870e6c4739bcf62f8185aee86c/e30cfc870e6c4739bcf62f8185aee86c.SD-480p-0.9Mbps-96249944.mp4'
    when 'luxlight-supreme-clay-lightener-7plus'
      assign official_video = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/vp/e207241d0bd34131b350c065e39d02da/e207241d0bd34131b350c065e39d02da.SD-480p-1.2Mbps-96249970.mp4'
    when 'luxlight-supreme-control-oil-lightening-system'
      assign official_video = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/vp/1aece978eff4458681e602d9ecefd390/1aece978eff4458681e602d9ecefd390.SD-480p-0.9Mbps-96249992.mp4'
    when 'luxlight-supreme-oil-developer-10vol', 'luxlight-supreme-oil-developer-20vol', 'luxlight-supreme-oil-developer-30vol'
      assign official_video = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/vp/a12d3d14d764410ea669ae262693b704/a12d3d14d764410ea669ae262693b704.SD-480p-0.9Mbps-96250012.mp4'
  endcase
  if use_official_gallery != true
    assign official_video = blank
  endif

  # Official h2 is the product name without the "HOP " brand prefix
  # ("Ultra Repair Shampoo"); display-only, the product title is untouched.
  assign display_title = product.title
  if is_hop_ultra_repair
    assign display_title = product.title | remove_first: 'HOP '
  endif

  # Official breadcrumb is two separate crumbs ("Tratamiento" / "Champú"),
  # rendered above the grid at the left edge, not inside the details column.
  assign crumbs = blank
  if is_hop_ultra_repair and taxonomy != blank
    assign crumbs = taxonomy | split: ' | '
  endif

  # UNDER's own eyebrow/title casing is "Under" (capitalized), not
  # lowercase like Luxlight's stylized "luxlight" wordmark — confirmed live
  # against all 4 official pages. `range_display` overrides the default
  # `| downcase` only for UNDER.
  assign range_display = range | downcase
  if is_under
    assign range_display = 'Under'
  endif
  # Official HOP Ultra Repair eyebrow reads "Ultra Repair" (confirmed live
  # on all 4 PDPs), not the generic lowercase "hop" wordmark — HOP's other
  # subfamilies (Colour Last/Keratin) are untouched, still "hop".
  if is_hop_family and subfamily != blank
    assign range_display = subfamily | replace: 'Color Last', 'Colour Last'
  endif

  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  # Mirror montibello-allied-stores.liquid's own offer resolution exactly —
  # a variant-level override list replaces the product-level list, and an
  # offer only counts when active AND it has a destination URL — so the CTA
  # only appears when the section it links to will actually render content.
  assign variant_offers = current_variant.metafields.montibello.allied_store_offers.value
  assign product_offers = product.metafields.montibello.allied_store_offers.value

  assign has_variant_offers = false
  for offer in variant_offers
    assign has_variant_offers = true
    break
  endfor

  assign allied_offers = product_offers
  if has_variant_offers
    assign allied_offers = variant_offers
  endif

  assign has_allied_offers = false
  for offer in allied_offers
    if offer.active.value == true and offer.product_url.value != blank
      assign has_allied_offers = true
    endif
  endfor

  assign show_format = false
  if current_variant.title != blank and current_variant.title != 'Default Title'
    assign show_format = true
  endif

  # Only a genuine choice between 2+ real values counts as a "selector" —
  # a single named option value (e.g. Luxlight's "Formato: 500 gr" after the
  # earlier format-tag data fix) is informational only and must fall through
  # to the plain icon row below, never render as a one-item clickable pill
  # group. Confirmed live: renaming a product's synthetic "Title" option
  # flips `has_only_default_variant` to false even with only one real value,
  # so that flag alone is not sufficient — the value count must be checked too.
  assign show_variant_selector = false
  if product.has_only_default_variant == false and product.options_with_values.size == 1 and product.options_with_values.first.values.size > 1
    assign show_variant_selector = true
  endif

  # A single-format product (the common Luxlight case) shows its format as
  # a plain icon row alongside hair_type/technology, never as a pill AND
  # never duplicated into a separate "Formato" group — that redundancy
  # (the same "500 gr" shown twice) was one of the confirmed visual-parity
  # bugs. A true multi-format product keeps its own pill selector below,
  # unaffected.
  assign show_format_row = false
  if show_format and show_variant_selector == false
    assign show_format_row = true
  endif

  # UNDER's official page never shows a hair-type row (confirmed live —
  # only "60 g"/"1000 ml" + the 3 accordions appear in the info stack) even
  # though the `hair_type` metafield IS populated on the activators with
  # genuinely useful text ("4,5% (15 vol.): Aclara hasta 1 tono...") —
  # that text simply isn't surfaced as a row on the official PDP. Per this
  # sprint's explicit "do not invent a hair-type row if the official page
  # does not show one" rule, it's suppressed for UNDER only; the metafield
  # itself is untouched (still available for HOP, which does show this row).
  assign show_hair_type_row = false
  if hair_type != blank and is_under == false
    assign show_hair_type_row = true
  endif

  # HOP Ultra Repair's official hero goes straight from the "Cabello dañado"
  # row into the 3 accordions — no `technology_description` bullet row
  # (confirmed live: that long LifeAlgae paragraph only appears, shorter and
  # rewritten, as the "LifeAlgae Bioscience" card in Ingredientes
  # principales further down). Rendering the same long paragraph a second
  # time as a top bullet row was never matched on the official page.
  assign show_technology_row = false
  if technology_description != blank and is_hop_family == false
    assign show_technology_row = true
  endif

  assign has_info_rows = false
  if show_hair_type_row or show_format_row or show_technology_row
    assign has_info_rows = true
  endif

  # --- Merged from the former montibello-product-details.liquid section ---
  assign features = product.metafields.montibello.features.value
  assign how_to_use_field = product.metafields.montibello.how_to_use
  assign how_to_use = how_to_use_field.value
  assign full_ingredients_field = product.metafields.montibello.full_ingredients
  assign ingredients = full_ingredients_field.value
  assign interest_data_field = product.metafields.montibello.interest_data
  assign interest_data = interest_data_field.value
  assign technical_data_field = product.metafields.montibello.technical_data
  assign technical_data = technical_data_field.value
  assign technology_heading = product.metafields.montibello.technology_heading.value
  assign claim_footnote = product.metafields.montibello.claim_footnote.value

  # UNDER 4-PDP official parity pass: UNDER's `features` metaobject is
  # already rendered as the full editorial photo-row further down the page
  # (sections/montibello-product-benefits.liquid, which the montibello
  # template also includes) — rendering it a SECOND time here as a plain
  # bullet-list "Ver características" accordion produced a duplicate the
  # official page doesn't have (confirmed live: exactly 3 accordions, no
  # 4th). Excluded alongside HOP/LUXLIGHT, which already had their own
  # reasons not to show this accordion.
  assign has_features = false
  if range != 'HOP' and range != 'LUXLIGHT' and range != 'UNDER'
    for feature in features
      assign has_features = true
      break
    endfor
  endif

  assign has_technology_block = false
  if technology_heading != blank or technology_description != blank
    assign has_technology_block = true
  endif
  if range == 'HOP' or range == 'LUXLIGHT'
    assign has_technology_block = false
  endif

  # UNDER's official page shows exactly 3 accordions (ingredients/how-to/
  # datos de interés) — no separate "Datos técnicos" row (confirmed live).
  # The `technical_data` metafield content (mix ratios, etc.) stays intact
  # on the product for any other use; only its accordion render is hidden.
  assign show_technical_data = true
  if range == 'LUXLIGHT' or range == 'UNDER'
    assign show_technical_data = false
  endif

  assign has_info_stack = false
  if has_features or how_to_use != blank or ingredients != blank or interest_data != blank or has_technology_block or claim_footnote != blank
    assign has_info_stack = true
  endif
  if show_technical_data and technical_data != blank
    assign has_info_stack = true
  endif
%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
  {{ product | structured_data }}
</script>

<div
  class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} montibello-pdp-main{% if is_luxlight %} montibello-pdp-main--luxlight{% endif %}{% if is_under %} montibello-pdp-main--under{% endif %}{% if is_hop_ultra_repair %} montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair{% endif %} spacing-style"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
>
  {% if crumbs != blank %}
    <ul class="montibello-pdp-main__crumbs">
      {% for crumb in crumbs %}
        <li class="montibello-pdp-main__crumb">{{ crumb }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="montibello-pdp-main__grid">
    <div class="montibello-pdp-main__media montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--1">
      {% if use_official_gallery %}
        <div class="montibello-ur-gallery" data-montibello-ur-gallery>
          <ul class="montibello-ur-gallery__thumbs" style="--ur-thumbs: {% liquid
                if official_video != blank
                  assign thumb_count = official_gallery.size | plus: 1
                else
                  assign thumb_count = official_gallery.size
                endif
                if thumb_count < 5
                  assign thumb_count = 5
                endif
              %}{{ thumb_count }}">
            {% for file in official_gallery %}
              <li>
                <button type="button" class="montibello-ur-gallery__thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}" data-ur-thumb="{{ forloop.index0 }}" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} {{ forloop.index }}">
                  <img src="{{ file | strip | asset_url }}" alt="" width="66" height="93" loading="lazy">
                </button>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
            {% if official_video != blank %}
              <li>
                <button type="button" class="montibello-ur-gallery__thumb" data-ur-thumb="{{ official_gallery.size }}" aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} — vídeo">
                  <img src="{{ 'official-pdp-video-thumb.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="66" height="93" loading="lazy">
                </button>
              </li>
            {% endif %}
          </ul>
          <div class="montibello-ur-gallery__stage">
            {% if range == 'LUXLIGHT' %}<span class="montibello-nuevo-badge">nuevo</span>{% endif %}
            {% for file in official_gallery %}
              <img
                class="montibello-ur-gallery__slide{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"
                src="{{ file | strip | asset_url }}"
                alt="{{ product.title | escape }}"
                width="1600"
                height="2239"
                {% unless forloop.first %}loading="lazy"{% endunless %}
                data-ur-slide="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
              >
            {% endfor %}
            {% if official_video != blank %}
              <video
                class="montibello-ur-gallery__slide montibello-ur-gallery__slide--video"
                src="{{ official_video }}"
                width="1600"
                height="2239"
                muted
                loop
                playsinline
                preload="none"
                data-ur-slide="{{ official_gallery.size }}"
                aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} — vídeo"
              ></video>
            {% endif %}
            <button type="button" class="montibello-ur-gallery__arrow montibello-ur-gallery__arrow--prev" data-ur-prev aria-label="Anterior" hidden>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="montibello-ur-gallery__arrow montibello-ur-gallery__arrow--next" data-ur-next aria-label="Siguiente">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% else %}
        {% content_for 'block', type: '_product-media-gallery', id: 'media-gallery', closest.product: product %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="montibello-pdp-main__details">
      {% if taxonomy != blank and crumbs == blank %}
        <p class="montibello-pdp-main__taxonomy montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--2">{{ taxonomy }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if range != blank %}
        <p class="montibello-pdp-main__eyebrow montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--2">{{ range_display }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      <h2 class="montibello-pdp-main__title montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--2">{{ display_title }}</h2>

      {% if functional_subtitle != blank %}
        <h1 class="montibello-pdp-main__subtitle{% if functional_subtitle.size > 60 %} montibello-pdp-main__subtitle--long{% endif %} montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--2">{{ functional_subtitle }}</h1>
      {% endif %}

      {% if product.description != blank %}
        <div class="montibello-pdp-main__description montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--3">{{ product.description }}</div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if professional_only %}
        <p class="montibello-pdp-main__professional montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--3">Exclusivo Profesional</p>
      {% endif %}

      {% if is_hop_ultra_repair and use_official_gallery %}
        {% comment %}
          Mobile only (hidden on desktop by CSS): the official mobile PDP collapses
          the hair-type row + the three accordions behind a bold "Ver características"
          bar. Pure presentation toggle, no data of its own.
        {% endcomment %}
        <button type="button" class="montibello-pdp-main__features-toggle" data-ur-features-toggle aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Ver características</span>
          <span class="montibello-pdp-main__features-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'montibello-luxlight-icon', icon: 'arrow_long' %}</span>
        </button>
      {% endif %}

      {% if has_info_rows %}
        <div class="montibello-pdp-main__info-rows montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--4">
          {% comment %}
            ROW ORDER (Luxlight copy audit pass): official Spain order is
            Format → Hair type → Technology, confirmed live via DOM order on
            every one of the 8 official PDPs (format-icon.svg row, then
            icono-tipo-de-cabello.svg row, then icono-ingrediente-
            principal.svg row). This used to render Hair type before Format
            — swapped to match.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% if show_format_row %}
            <div class="montibello-pdp-main__info-row">
              <span class="montibello-pdp-main__info-icon{% if use_official_icons %} montibello-pdp-main__info-icon--official{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">
                {% if use_official_icons %}
                  {% render 'montibello-luxlight-icon', icon: 'format' %}
                {% else %}
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">{% render 'icon', icon: 'box' %}</svg>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
              <span>{{ current_variant.title }}</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if show_hair_type_row %}
            <div class="montibello-pdp-main__info-row">
              <span class="montibello-pdp-main__info-icon{% if use_official_icons %} montibello-pdp-main__info-icon--official{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">
                {% if use_official_icons %}
                  {% render 'montibello-luxlight-icon', icon: 'hair_type' %}
                {% else %}
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">{% render 'icon', icon: 'leaf' %}</svg>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
              <span>{{ hair_type }}</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if show_technology_row %}
            <div class="montibello-pdp-main__info-row">
              <span class="montibello-pdp-main__info-icon{% if use_official_icons %} montibello-pdp-main__info-icon--official{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">
                {% if use_official_icons %}
                  {% render 'montibello-luxlight-icon', icon: 'technology' %}
                {% else %}
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">{% render 'icon', icon: 'lock' %}</svg>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
              <span>{{ technology_description_field | metafield_tag }}</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% if show_variant_selector %}
        <div class="montibello-pdp-main__variants">
          {% for option in product.options_with_values %}
            {% assign option_index = option.position | minus: 1 %}
            <fieldset class="montibello-pdp-main__variant-group">
              <legend class="montibello-pdp-main__variant-label">{{ option.name }}</legend>
              <div class="montibello-pdp-main__variant-pills">
                {% for value in option.values %}
                  {% for variant in product.variants %}
                    {% if variant.options[option_index] == value %}
                      <a
                        href="{{ product.url }}?variant={{ variant.id }}"
                        class="montibello-pdp-main__variant-pill{% if variant.id == current_variant.id %} is-selected{% endif %}"
                        {% if variant.id == current_variant.id %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                      >
                        {{ value }}
                      </a>
                      {% break %}
                    {% endif %}
                  {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </fieldset>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %}
        Primary non-ecommerce purchase-path CTA. Peru has no direct
        checkout, so this always points to the informational
        /pages/donde-comprar page — unconditional, unlike the "Tiendas
        aliadas" CTA above it used to be (that one required
        allied_store_offers data that doesn't exist yet for any product).

        HIDDEN FOR LUXLIGHT (copy audit pass): the official Luxlight hero
        info-stack has no purchase CTA interrupting the flow — it goes
        straight from the bullet rows into the accordion rows. Removed from
        the Luxlight hero presentation ONLY; `/pages/donde-comprar` itself
        is untouched and still linked from HOP/UNDER PDPs and everywhere
        else it already appeared.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% comment %}
        HIDDEN FOR UNDER too (UNDER 4-PDP official parity pass): a live DOM
        audit of all 4 official Under PDPs found no "Dónde comprar" CTA in
        the hero info stack (same flow as Luxlight — bullet rows straight
        into the accordion rows). `/pages/donde-comprar` itself is
        untouched and still linked from HOP.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% comment %}
        HIDDEN FOR HOP ULTRA REPAIR too (TRUE OFFICIAL PARITY FINAL pass): a
        live audit of all 4 official Ultra Repair PDPs found no "Dónde
        comprar" CTA in the info stack — Spain's own buy flow / country-
        availability notice sits there instead, which Peru doesn't
        replicate (no real checkout). Scoped to the 4 Ultra Repair products
        only; HOP's other subfamilies (Colour Last/Keratin) keep this CTA
        unchanged.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% if range != 'LUXLIGHT' and range != 'UNDER' and is_hop_ultra_repair == false %}
        <a href="/pages/donde-comprar" class="montibello-pdp-main__cta">
          Dónde comprar
        </a>
      {% endif %}

      {% if has_allied_offers %}
        <a href="#montibello-allied-stores-{{ product.id }}" class="montibello-pdp-main__cta montibello-pdp-main__cta--secondary">
          Tiendas aliadas
        </a>
      {% endif %}

      {% comment %}
        Info stack — accordion rows, technology block, footnote. Merged in
        from the former montibello-product-details.liquid section so it
        stays inside THIS right column, directly below the CTAs — see the
        INFO STACK MERGE comment above.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% if has_info_stack %}
        <div class="montibello-pdp-main__info-stack montibello-pdp-main__enter montibello-pdp-main__enter--5">
          {% if has_technology_block %}
            <div class="montibello-pdp-main__technology">
              {% if technology_heading != blank %}
                <h2 class="montibello-pdp-main__technology-heading">{{ technology_heading }}</h2>
              {% endif %}
              {% if technology_description != blank %}
                <div class="montibello-pdp-main__technology-description">{{ technology_description_field | metafield_tag }}</div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          {% endif %}

          <div class="montibello-pdp-main__accordion">
            {% if ingredients != blank %}
              {% assign ingredients_tag = full_ingredients_field | metafield_tag %}
              {% capture ingredients_content %}<div class="montibello-pdp-main__ingredients">{{ ingredients_tag }}</div>{% endcapture %}
              {% if use_official_icons %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: 'Ver todos los ingredientes', content: ingredients_content, icon: 'ingredients', icon_source: 'official', arrow: arrow_style %}
              {% else %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: 'Ver todos los ingredientes', content: ingredients_content, icon: 'clipboard' %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}

            {% if how_to_use != blank %}
              {% comment %}
                Official pages use the RANGE wordmark here, not the product
                name — confirmed live: "Cómo usar luxlight" (Supreme
                Lightener 9+) and "Cómo usar Under" (all 4 Under PDPs,
                including the activators — same fixed label regardless of
                strength, confirmed against all 4 official pages). Other
                ranges keep the previous product.title behavior until
                independently verified.
              {% endcomment %}
              {% if range == 'LUXLIGHT' %}
                {% assign how_to_use_label = 'Cómo usar luxlight' %}
              {% elsif range == 'UNDER' %}
                {% assign how_to_use_label = 'Cómo usar Under' %}
              {% elsif is_hop_ultra_repair and subfamily != blank %}
                {% comment %}
                  Official reads "Cómo usar Ultra Repair" on all 4 PDPs —
                  the SUBFAMILY name, not the individual product title
                  (confirmed live, same fixed-label pattern as Luxlight/
                  Under above).
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {% assign how_to_use_label = 'Cómo usar ' | append: subfamily | replace: 'Color Last', 'Colour Last' %}
              {% else %}
                {% assign how_to_use_label = 'Cómo usar ' | append: product.title %}
              {% endif %}
              {% assign how_to_use_tag = how_to_use_field | metafield_tag %}
              {% if use_official_icons %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: how_to_use_label, content: how_to_use_tag, icon: 'how_to', icon_source: 'official', arrow: arrow_style %}
              {% else %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: how_to_use_label, content: how_to_use_tag, icon: 'bottle' %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}

            {% if interest_data != blank %}
              {% assign interest_data_tag = interest_data_field | metafield_tag %}
              {% if use_official_icons %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: 'Datos de interés', content: interest_data_tag, icon: 'interest_data', icon_source: 'official', arrow: arrow_style %}
              {% else %}
                {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: 'Datos de interés', content: interest_data_tag, icon: 'question_mark' %}
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}

            {% if show_technical_data and technical_data != blank %}
              {% assign technical_data_tag = technical_data_field | metafield_tag %}
              {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: 'Datos técnicos', content: technical_data_tag, icon: 'question_mark' %}
            {% endif %}

            {% if has_features %}
              {% capture features_content %}
                <ul class="montibello-pdp-main__feature-list">
                  {% for feature in features %}
                    <li>
                      {% if feature.title.value != blank %}<strong>{{ feature.title.value }}:</strong>{% endif %}
                      {% if feature.description.value != blank %}
                        {{ feature.description | metafield_tag }}
                      {% endif %}
                    </li>
                  {% endfor %}
                </ul>
              {% endcapture %}
              {% render 'montibello-pdp-accordion-item', label: 'Ver características', content: features_content, icon: 'clipboard' %}
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          {% if claim_footnote != blank %}
            <p class="montibello-pdp-main__footnote">{{ claim_footnote }}</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% if is_hop_ultra_repair %}
  {% style %}
    @font-face { font-family: 'TTCommons'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ 'tt-commons-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'TTCommons'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ 'tt-commons-medium.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'TTCommons'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ 'tt-commons-demibold.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
    @font-face { font-family: 'TTCommons'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; src: url('{{ 'tt-commons-bold.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2'); }
  {% endstyle %}
{% endif %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .montibello-pdp-main__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 20px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 60px;
      padding-inline: 30px;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main__media {
    /* Flush against the page background, no gray/beige box — the official
       gallery sits on plain white with no container background at all. */
    background: transparent;
    /* Manager-feedback closure pass: switching the native gallery block to
       `media_presentation: carousel` (fixing the "giant image" bug) lays
       every slide out side-by-side in a track wider than the viewport and
       translates it to show the active one — correct off-viewport slides
       were bleeding out and causing real horizontal page overflow at
       mobile widths (measured 1008px scrollWidth on a 390px viewport, all
       other slides visible past the right edge). Clipping here contains
       the track without touching the native gallery component itself. */
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* PACKSHOT SCALE (UNDER 4-PDP official parity pass, P0 #1): measured live
     via getBoundingClientRect() — the native gallery's `aspect_ratio:
     "adapt"` setting sizes the media box to the SOURCE photo's own
     intrinsic ratio at full column width, and Under's tube/cream packshots
     (e.g. under-tubo.png, a tall 720×1336 crop) are far more elongated than
     the official Spain photography at that same "adapt" full-width
     treatment — measured 615×820px before this fix (the image alone taller
     than the entire right-column text stack, confirmed against the
     official page's own rendered packshot at 546×764px in a wider column).
     The whole size chain (media-gallery → slideshow-slide →
     .product-media's own inline `aspect-ratio`) is driven by the WIDTH this
     outer container provides, so capping max-width here (not max-height)
     lets every descendant recompute proportionally with zero cropping
     (`object-fit: cover` never has to crop when the box ratio already
     matches the image's own ratio) — the packshot shrinks as a whole,
     stays centered, and the text column stops feeling dominated. */
  .montibello-pdp-main--under .montibello-pdp-main__media {
    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      /* `width` (not `max-width` + `margin-inline: auto`) — a grid item
         with auto margins switches to shrink-to-fit sizing per spec, which
         made its own `width: 100%` descendants (the native gallery's
         percentage-width chain) resolve against an indefinite containing
         block and collapse to 0 (confirmed live: computed width 0px,
         packshot disappeared entirely). A definite `width` avoids that
         circularity; `justify-self: center` centers it in the grid track. */
      width: 300px;
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }

  /* PACKSHOT SCALE (HOP ULTRA REPAIR — TRUE OFFICIAL PARITY FINAL): the
     official photography already bakes generous white space around the
     bottle/jar/tube INTO the source image at full column width — Peru's
     own product photos are tight crops with no such built-in margin, so at
     the same full-column "adapt" treatment the packshot reads as "too
     close"/zoomed in (measured live: the shampoo bottle's media box was
     614.5×944px, filling the entire column edge to edge). Same root cause
     and same fix shape as the UNDER packshot-scale fix above (a definite
     `width`, not `max-width + margin-inline:auto`, to avoid the grid-item
     shrink-to-fit 0-width bug documented there) — just a lighter reduction,
     since HOP's packshots aren't as extremely elongated as UNDER's were.
     Scoped to the 4 real Ultra Repair products only. */
  /* (superseded by the official gallery below — the old 420px cap only
     existed to fake whitespace around Peru's tight crops; the official
     canvases carry their own whitespace.) */

  /* ===== HOP ULTRA REPAIR — forensic official layout (1440 measurements from
     hair.montibello.com/producto/ultra-repair-shampoo): content 1300px
     centred, two 630px columns with a 40px gap; gallery = 66px thumbnail
     column + 18px gap + 546x764 stage (1600:2239 canvas); right column
     starts level with the stage top. Everything is scoped to the modifier
     so every other range keeps its previous CSS untouched. ===== */
  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair {
    font-family: 'TTCommons', 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
    color: #000;
    background-color: #f6f6f3 !important;
    /* full-bleed beige band without touching the section wrapper markup */
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 100vmax #f6f6f3;
    clip-path: inset(0 -100vmax);
    padding-block: 50px 25px !important;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair * {
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__crumbs {
    display: flex;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1300px;
    margin: 0 auto 24px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 20px;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #767676;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding: 0;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__crumb + .montibello-pdp-main__crumb {
    position: relative;
    margin-left: 20px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__crumb + .montibello-pdp-main__crumb::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -10px;
    top: 3px;
    bottom: 3px;
    width: 1px;
    background: rgba(118, 118, 118, 0.45);
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__grid {
    max-width: 1300px;
    padding-inline: 20px;
    gap: 32px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: 630px 630px;
      gap: 40px;
      padding-inline: 0;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__media {
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: 66px 546px;
      gap: 18px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__thumbs {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    order: 2;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    overflow-x: auto;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      order: 0;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 15px;
      overflow: visible;
    }
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__thumb {
    display: block;
    flex: none;
    width: 66px;
    height: 93px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 5px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__thumb img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__stage {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 1600 / 2239;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__slide {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__slide--video {
    object-fit: contain;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__slide.is-active {
    opacity: 1;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__arrow {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: 8px;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: #000;
    cursor: pointer;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      right: -50px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__arrow--prev {
    right: auto;
    left: 8px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      left: -50px;
    }
  }

  /* official arrow is effectively invisible on the beige canvas until the
     gallery is hovered — keep the control reachable, show it on hover/focus */
  .montibello-ur-gallery__arrow {
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery:hover .montibello-ur-gallery__arrow,
  .montibello-ur-gallery__arrow:focus-visible {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .montibello-ur-gallery__arrow[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* right column — official vertical rhythm (all values measured) */
  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__details {
    gap: 0;
    position: static;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__eyebrow {
    order: 1;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-size: 23px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 21px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    opacity: 1;
    color: #000;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__title {
    order: 2;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 40px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 40px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-transform: capitalize;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__subtitle {
    order: 3;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    opacity: 1;
    color: #000;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__description {
    order: 4;
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 19.7px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__description p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__description p + p {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  /* "Exclusivo Profesional" sits under the description in the official red */
  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__professional {
    order: 5;
    margin: 20px 0 -20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 19.7px;
    color: rgb(225, 53, 62);
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__variants {
    order: 5;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__variant-label {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__variant-pills {
    margin-top: 0;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__variant-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 39px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    border: 0.5px solid #000;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: transparent;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: #000;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__variant-pill.is-selected {
    background: transparent;
    color: #000;
    border-width: 1.5px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__features-toggle {
    display: none;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* official mobile (390): 15px gutters, 35/35 title, thumbs in a 5-up row,
       and the hair/accordion stack collapsed behind "Ver características" */
    .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair {
      padding-inline: 0 !important;
      padding-block-start: 30px !important;
    }

    .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__crumbs,
    .montibello-pdp-main--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-main__grid {
      padding-inline: 0;
